<p>(a) During the second quarter of 1995, the company incurred severance costs of $950,000 resulting in a charge to net income of $550,000 or $.09 per share after related tax benefit.</p>
<p>(b) The company elected to complete the amortization of the gain on sale of company routes during the fourth quarter of 1995.  Results for the 1995 quarter and year-to-date include the amortization of the gain on sale of company routes which totaled $1,731,727 and $3,162,033, respectively, and increased net income by $988,770 or $.16 per share and $1,751,577 or $.28 per share, respectively.</p>
<p>(c) During the third quarter of 1995, the company was required to record a tax charge of approximately $551,000 or $.09 per share.  This charge was due to the remeasuring of the company's deferred tax asset in accordance with SFAS No. 109 to reflect a decrease in the statutory state tax rate.</p>
